\subsection{Deciding non-interactively}
\label{sec:sessions-decide}

With [[search -n]] persisting sessions headlessly
(\cref{sec:search-session-persist}), the one remaining step that forced the
TUI open was recording the keep/discard decisions themselves.  [[sessions
decide]] closes that gap so the full review loop---search, screen, decide,
export---can run scripted or agent-driven
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/66}).

Papers are selected by DOI or by the session's paper id (the same id
[[sessions show --format json]] and the provenance tooling expose; it falls
back to a title-author hash when a paper has no DOI, so every paper is
addressable).  Both selectors are repeatable and can be mixed, and DOIs
compare case-insensitively since registries treat them so.

Two invariants mirror the TUI rather than trusting the caller:
\begin{description}
\item[Discarding requires a motivation] [[ReviewDecision.is_valid]] demands
  at least one tag on a discarded paper, so we refuse [[--discard]] without
  [[--tag]] up front instead of saving a session the TUI would consider
  invalid.
\item[All or nothing] If \emph{any} selector matches no paper in the
  session, nothing is saved and the exit code is nonzero.  A typo in one DOI
  of a batch must not leave the session half-updated---scripts can fix the
  selector and simply rerun.
\end{description}
Tags accumulate via [[add_tag]] (idempotent), so redeciding a paper refines
rather than clobbers its tags; the status change itself is an overwrite,
which is what redeciding means.

<<sessions command>>=
@sessions_app.command("decide")
def sessions_decide(
    name: Annotated[
        str,
        typer.Argument(
            help="Session name or query to record decisions in.",
            autocompletion=complete_session_name,
        ),
    ],
    keep: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option("--keep", help="Mark the selected papers as kept."),
    ] = False,
    discard: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--discard",
            help="Mark the selected papers as discarded (requires --tag).",
        ),
    ] = False,
    doi: Annotated[
        Optional[list[str]],
        typer.Option(
            "--doi",
            help="Select a paper by DOI (case-insensitive). Repeatable.",
        ),
    ] = None,
    paper_id: Annotated[
        Optional[list[str]],
        typer.Option(
            "--paper-id",
            help="Select a paper by its session paper id. Repeatable.",
            autocompletion=complete_session_paper_id,
        ),
    ] = None,
    tag: Annotated[
        Optional[list[str]],
        typer.Option(
            "--tag", "-t",
            help="Tag to attach: theme (kept) or motivation (discarded). "
                 "Repeatable.",
        ),
    ] = None,
) -> None:
    """
    Record keep/discard decisions in a saved session, without the TUI.

    Select papers by --doi and/or --paper-id (both repeatable). Discarding
    requires at least one --tag as motivation. If any selector matches
    nothing, no changes are saved and the exit code is nonzero.

    Example:
        scholar sessions decide my-review --keep --doi 10.1145/3568813 \\
            --tag misconceptions
    """
    from scholar.review import (
        DecisionStatus, ReviewSource, load_session, save_session,
    )

    console = Console()
    <<validate decide options>>

    session = load_session(name)
    if session is None:
        console.print(f"[red]Session not found: {escape(name)}[/red]")
        raise typer.Exit(1)

    <<select decisions by doi and paper id>>

    status = DecisionStatus.KEPT if keep else DecisionStatus.DISCARDED
    for decision in selected.values():
        decision.status = status
        decision.source = ReviewSource.HUMAN
        for t in tag or []:
            decision.add_tag(t)

    save_session(session)
    word = "kept" if keep else "discarded"
    console.print(
        f"[green]{len(selected)} paper(s) marked {word}[/green] "
        f"in session '{escape(name)}'"
    )
@

The option validation happens before the session is even loaded, so a
malformed invocation cannot depend on session state:

<<validate decide options>>=
if keep == discard:
    console.print("[red]Specify exactly one of --keep or --discard.[/red]")
    raise typer.Exit(1)
if not doi and not paper_id:
    console.print(
        "[red]Select at least one paper with --doi or --paper-id.[/red]"
    )
    raise typer.Exit(1)
if discard and not tag:
    console.print(
        "[red]--discard requires at least one --tag (motivation).[/red]"
    )
    raise typer.Exit(1)
@

Selection collects matches into a dict keyed by paper id, which both
deduplicates (the same paper may be named by DOI \emph{and} id) and gives a
stable count for the summary.  Unmatched selectors are gathered rather than
failing fast so one run reports \emph{all} typos:

<<select decisions by doi and paper id>>=
by_doi = {
    d.paper.doi.strip().lower(): d
    for d in session.decisions
    if d.paper.doi
}
by_id = {d.paper.id: d for d in session.decisions}

selected = {}
missing = []
for value in doi or []:
    decision = by_doi.get(value.strip().lower())
    if decision is None:
        missing.append(f"DOI {value}")
    else:
        selected[decision.paper.id] = decision
for value in paper_id or []:
    decision = by_id.get(value)
    if decision is None:
        missing.append(f"paper id {value}")
    else:
        selected[decision.paper.id] = decision

if missing:
    for entry in missing:
        console.print(f"[red]Not in session: {escape(entry)}[/red]")
    console.print("[yellow]No changes saved.[/yellow]")
    raise typer.Exit(1)
